  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The Peshitta family has samekh (SEDRA lexemes 2102–2105). Its uses for washing and bathing explain why the same verb occurs both at the shipwreck and at the washing of feet. The Aramaic letter does not distinguish the older sounds behind ח. The proposed Akkadian comparison remains uncertain."
